From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:10:59 +0530
Subject: Migrate to CppInterOp's typed handle API

CppInterOp replaced the interchangeable `void*` aliases with distinct
handle structs, so the old spellings no longer name anything and decls and
types no longer convert into each other:

  - Cpp::TInterp_t   -> Cpp::InterpRef  (and createInterpreter returns one
                        rather than laundering it through void*)
  - Cpp::TCppScope_t -> Cpp::DeclRef
  - Cpp::TCppType_t  -> Cpp::TypeRef
  - naming a type goes through GetTypeAsString; GetQualifiedName and
    GetQualifiedCompleteName now take a decl only
  - Evaluate returns a typed Cpp::Box, so unbox the C++ version as int

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b0b3e66c36f2dfb8b355fcfad9e83275d32d6919)
